{"ts": "2026-11-03T18:29:13.990529Z", "run_id": "r-20261103T1827Z-6d81", "unit": "openspec:add-dbos-runtime", "seq": 7, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-018", "target": "F-233c28d7", "decision": "accept", "by": "agent", "reason": "the redaction serves a stricter clause of the same scenario. spec.md:19 also requires that within 5 s of the pool-error test no log line holds 'terminating connection'. DBOS 5.3.0 itself logs `Unexpected error in system database client: ${err}` (system_database.js:180 and 184), where a pg error stringifies as 'error: terminating connection …' and can carry a host. Forwarding String(entry) unchanged would break that clause and put driver text in the logs. The literal 'String(entry)' in spec.md:19 and design.md:9 conflicts with that clause. A follow-up amends the spec text to: the adapter forwards String(entry), with a lowercase pg 'error: …' tail replaced by 'error: [redacted]'. Verified by the orchestrator against the spec and the SDK source.", "text_sha256": "4818965febd714306bf5c5bf5771e1088cb1d24bc1344931791625c0a923cf36", "answer_sha256": "18f9742c093c872f83b16a445847f418382e8c9b63cb5f72b08e93d8f3d49784", "marker": "CLAUDECODE"}
{"ts": "2026-11-03T18:29:13.991474Z", "run_id": "r-20261103T1827Z-6d81", "unit": "openspec:add-dbos-runtime", "seq": 8, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-019", "target": "F-1216922b", "decision": "reject", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding holds. In src/durable/steps.ts the JSON check of fn's result and the after observer call sit inside the per-attempt try whose catch counts an attempt and loops, so with retries above 0 and no retryable predicate an after observer that throws, or a non-JSON result, makes fn run again after it already succeeded. Design decision 6 says fn runs up to retries plus one times, the result is then checked, the after observer runs once, and an observer that throws fails the step; the spec says only fn is retried while retryable allows. Only errors thrown by fn itself may be retried. WHEN runStep runs with retries 2 and fn resolves a valid DurableJson but the after observer throws THEN fn has run exactly once, the step rejects with the observer's error unchanged and no second attempt of fn is made.", "text_sha256": "ba2545cfc2bfef7fdfedf5dec976fcf13b0e18de8cc48700c3b6e532d6ce6083", "answer_sha256": "30961dd4ac81fdb6e47855718543805898f32b04cc9cae141f7a59bc3bff18c7", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
